From: Herman Brule <contact@herman-brule.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:10:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ubus: release the previous request prototype

uc_ubus_handle_reply_common() hangs each served call's request
prototype (its args and info objects, refcount 1) on the SHARED
"ubus.request" type prototype with ucv_prototype_set(), which
overwrites ->proto without releasing the one already there. Every
call served by a ucode ubus object therefore orphans the previous
call's prototype, and only the garbage collector could reclaim it;
netifd never enables it.

Measured on an RTL9607F board (netifd 2026.04.23, ucode 2026.04.24),
netifd RssAnon: 600 x `ubus call network.wireless status` +2476 kB,
600 more +2524 kB (linear), 600 x `get_validate` +2720 kB, while the
C-served `network.interface.wan status` and `network.device status`
stayed flat. A poller at one call a minute leaks ~250 kB/h.

Release the old prototype before setting the new one. With it, the
same 600 status calls leave netifd at 812 -> 812 kB, and hostapd's
ucode object at 764 -> 764 kB.

Signed-off-by: Herman Brule <contact@herman-brule.com>
---

--- a/lib/ubus.c
+++ b/lib/ubus.c
@@ -2450,8 +2450,12 @@
 	/* fd is copied to deferred request. ensure it does not get closed early */
 	ubus_request_get_caller_fd(req);
 
-	if (reqproto)
-		ucv_prototype_set(ucv_prototype_get(reqobj), reqproto);
+	if (reqproto) {
+		uc_value_t *typeproto = ucv_prototype_get(reqobj);
+
+		ucv_put(ucv_prototype_get(typeproto));
+		ucv_prototype_set(typeproto, reqproto);
+	}
 
 	/* push object context, handler and request object onto stack */
 	uc_vm_stack_push(vm, ucv_get(this));
